# =============================================================================
# CODEOWNERS — 19May_2 DevOps Platform Reference Architecture
# =============================================================================
#
# This file declares the path-based reviewer assignment for the repository.
# When a pull request modifies files matching one of the patterns below,
# the listed teams are automatically requested as reviewers, and (when
# branch protection is configured with "Require review from Code Owners")
# their approval is required before the PR can be merged.
#
# Spec & syntax reference:
#   https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositories-settings-and-customization/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Notes about syntax — important when editing this file:
#   * Each non-comment line has the form: <path-pattern> @owner [@owner ...].
#   * Patterns use gitignore-style globs anchored at the repository root.
#   * A leading slash ("/") anchors the pattern to the repository root.
#   * A trailing slash ("/") matches everything inside that directory,
#     recursively (i.e. "/docs/" is equivalent to "/docs/**").
#   * Comments must start at the beginning of a line — do NOT append a
#     trailing comment after a pattern, because the GitHub CODEOWNERS
#     parser is known to handle that inconsistently.
#   * The **last matching pattern wins**, so this file is sorted
#     general-to-specific: the global default sits at the very top,
#     top-level directory ownership comes next, and the more granular
#     sub-directory overrides come last.
#
# Placeholder teams — replace before enabling branch protection:
#   The team handles below (@19May_2/<team>) are notional placeholders.
#   Each adopter of this reference architecture is expected to substitute
#   real team handles or individual usernames belonging to their GitHub
#   organization before enabling "Require review from Code Owners" on
#   the protected branches. The organization name "19May_2" mirrors the
#   repository identity declared in §1.1 of the technical specification.
#
# Notional team responsibilities:
#   @19May_2/platform-maintainers   Overall stewardship of the platform
#                                   reference architecture; final review
#                                   on cross-cutting changes.
#   @19May_2/devex                  Developer experience: CI/CD pipelines,
#                                   reusable workflows, Backstage IDP,
#                                   working examples, scaffolding.
#   @19May_2/docs                   Documentation site, MkDocs config,
#                                   glossary, onboarding, getting-started.
#   @19May_2/architecture           Architecture decision records (ADRs)
#                                   and component-map narrative docs.
#   @19May_2/sre                    Observability, SLOs, runbooks,
#                                   incident response, progressive delivery.
#   @19May_2/infra                  Cloud infrastructure: Terraform/OpenTofu
#                                   modules, Crossplane providers, IaC scan.
#   @19May_2/security               Supply chain, secrets, policy-as-code,
#                                   security disclosure, IaC security scan.
#   @19May_2/product                Product owners — co-own SLOs and any
#                                   user-facing service-level commitments.
#   @19May_2/finops                 Cost allocation, budgets, OpenCost
#                                   dashboards and team-level chargeback.
#
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Global default — every file not matched by a more specific pattern below
# is owned by the platform maintainers. This entry MUST stay at the top
# because every later (more specific) pattern overrides it.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

*                                       @19May_2/platform-maintainers

